The CPS on my Windows 10 machine didn't exit properly. After installing it and updating the firmware of my GD77 and MD-UV380 (and database) I exited the CPS and loaded my NixOS VM and I started to hear my CPU fan start to run occasionally. Checked the Windows task manager after BTOP in the VM and the CPS was still running and taking up 30% CPU, so I ended the process. Consequently, Win 10 is buggy with hooking the radios up when VMWare is running, so I exit VMWare when using the CPS. Anyone else see the CPS continuing to run after closing it?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=673">WY7JT</a> — Fri Apr 12, 2024 3:34 pm</p><hr />
